.TH PYCDLIB-CATALOG 1 "Nov 2026" "pycdlib-catalog"

.SH NAME
pycdlib-catalog - generate file entity and path reference catalogs from an ISO using pycdlib

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pycdlib-catalog [OPTIONS] <iso-file>

.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a tool to catalog the entries on an existing ISO that carries one or
more of the ISO9660, Joliet, and Rock Ridge name spaces.  It emits three
catalogs:

.TP
.B file entities
One row per distinct on-disk data object.  Directory records that reference
the same data area (hard links, including across name spaces) collapse onto a
single entity, so a shared data area is counted once.

.TP
.B path references
One row per directory record in each name space.  The name is preserved
exactly as that name space stored it, so an ISO9660 name such as
"FOO.;1", its Rock Ridge name "foo", and its Joliet name can all appear
alongside one another.

.TP
.B shared extent conflicts
When two or more distinct entities reference the same non-empty data extent,
every directory record involved is listed here.  Name spaces are never paired
by display name; references only identify the same entity through the parsed
data object, so a conflict is reported with its directory records rather than
silently resolved by guessing.

.PP
Without \-output\-dir the three catalogs are written to standard output as
tab-separated tables with headings.  With \-output\-dir they are written to
the files entities.tsv, references.tsv, and conflicts.tsv in that directory.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-output\-dir " <destpath>"
The directory to write the three tab-separated catalog files to.  The
directory is created if it does not exist.  If not specified, the catalogs
are printed to standard output.

.SH SEE ALSO
pycdlib-explorer(1), pycdlib-extract-files(1), pycdlib-genisoimage(1)

